==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|flaxen}}, {{m|enm|flexon}}, {{m|enm|flexin}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fleaxen|t=of flax; flaxen}}, equivalent to {{af|en|flax|-en|id2=made of|t2=made of}}. Compare {{cog|nl|vlassen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈflæk.sən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-flaxen.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|æksən|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{head|en|adjective}}

# Made of or resembling [[flax]] fibers.
# {{lb|en|of hair}} A pale yellow brown as of dried flax; [[blonde]].
#: {{color panel|C2B280}}
#: ''The couple and their children have '''flaxen''' hair.''

